  ⚠ react(immutability): Cannot access variable while it is being initialized
   ╭─[immutability.tsx:6:15]
 5 │             setTimeout(() => {
 6 │               applyFilter();
   ·               ─────┬─────
   ·                    ╰── `applyFilter` is read during its own initialization
 7 │             });
   ╰────
  help: `applyFilter` is read while its declaration is still being initialized. Move the access after initialization. For a recursive callback, use a named function expression or restructure the callback so it does not capture itself during initialization
  note: React Compiler skipped optimizing this component or hook. Additional guidance: https://react.dev/reference/eslint-plugin-react-hooks/lints/immutability

